#
# The two keys that say where the tunnel check is asked, as image/gateway/render reads them
# from the env files (the first definition wins, an absent key takes the default written
# here): rendered by image/gateway/authorizer-start, so the authorizer listens where the
# data plane's bootstrap (envoy/gateway.yaml.in) dials and the host table (nftables.conf.in)
# agrees. The defaults here are those two templates' defaults, word for word: `make
# gateway-render-check` and image/gateway/check.sh fail when one of the three differs.
endpoint=@AUTHORIZER_ENDPOINT:-pipe: { path: /run/mediatore-gateway/check/check.sock }@
check_tcp=@CHECK_TCP_ELEMENTS:-@
